<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Runs BEFORE the main payload, and the ordering is the whole point.

  ★R5 — Event_Invitee__c.Contact__c / Lead__c and the XOR validation rule that
  reads them. These go first because the main payload rewrites the five things
  that depend on them: the four Invitee_* formulas stop reading Contact__r /
  Lead__r, Invitee_Type__c disappears entirely, and Invitee_Requires_Attendee
  replaces the XOR rule. A formula cannot be repointed while the field it names is
  still referenced by a validation rule, so the rule is dropped in the same pass.

  ★R5 — Account__c and Account_Owner__c. Neither has a source any more: an
  attendee has no Account, so a snapshot of one would be permanently blank. The
  Account snapshot is also read by the old Invitee_Org__c formula, which is why it
  belongs here rather than after.

  ★R3 — Exported_Count__c is a roll-up that filters on Status__c = 'Exported'. The
  main payload ships a Status__c picklist that no longer has that value, so if the
  field were still present when it landed, the deploy would fail on a filter
  referencing a value that no longer exists. Removing the roll-up first clears the
  way. Harmless to re-run against an org that never had R2.

  DATA WARNING: dropping Contact__c and Lead__c destroys the only record of who
  each existing invitee was. Migrate first — see Part 7 of DEPLOYMENT.md, which
  creates an Event_Attendee__c per invited Contact/Lead and back-fills
  Event_Attendee__c before this manifest runs.
-->
<Package xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <types>
        <members>Event_Invitee__c.Invitee_Is_Contact_Xor_Lead</members>
        <name>ValidationRule</name>
    </types>
    <types>
        <members>Event_Invitee__c.Contact__c</members>
        <members>Event_Invitee__c.Lead__c</members>
        <members>Event_Invitee__c.Account__c</members>
        <members>Event_Invitee__c.Account_Owner__c</members>
        <members>Marketing_Event__c.Exported_Count__c</members>
        <name>CustomField</name>
    </types>
    <version>61.0</version>
</Package>
